WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.189
- Please welcome Sabrina Carpenter.

00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:06.057
(audience cheer and clap)

00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:07.057
- Oh my God.

00:00:08.053 --> 00:00:09.805
This is very surreal.

00:00:09.805 --> 00:00:14.730
- It's such honor to have your
presence here on the show.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.000
You started at nine years old.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.833
- Yeah.

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:23.833
- So how did you know
yourself well enough at nine

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.710
to be in touch with what you could do?

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:29.570
- I don't think I knew anything.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.630
I think at nine years old,
you just love what you love

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.530
and you just gravitate towards
what you gravitate towards.

00:00:36.796 --> 00:00:37.629
I think for me,

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:39.790
I remember watching the
"Wizard of Oz" specifically,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.890
that was a very vivid memory
watching Judy Garland sing

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:47.300
just before I was nine
and I was just in awe.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.450
And I was like, "Oh, I wanna
do that forever if I can.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.690
- 'Cause if you started singing at nine,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.410
and putting yourself out there,
was there an earlier year,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.944
was there a moment in your life

00:00:56.944 --> 00:01:00.200
where you had the, I wanna do this moment?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.122
- Yeah well, I specifically remember

00:01:02.122 --> 00:01:04.950
there was a restaurant I went
to when I was six years old

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.760
and there was a waitress there, Patty,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.620
and it was her birthday.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.590
And I was like, "Oh, I wanna
sing happy birthday for you."

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.740
And so I sang her happy birthday.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.762
And then every time I came
back to that restaurant,

00:01:12.762 --> 00:01:14.460
she made me sing happy birthday

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.950
to anyone in the restaurant
who had a birthday,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.740
which some people started to gimme money.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.490
And I was like, "Oh!"

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.400
I was like, "Is this is my career?"

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.450
And I was six, so I didn't
really know what I was saying.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.560
My parents were like,
"You can't take that."

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.630
And I was like, "Are you sure?"

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.010
I was like, "'Cause this is my business."

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.270
- I mean, I'm so glad.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.130
Thank you, I was like, I
wanted to know a moment.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.706
I love that so much.

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:41.180
You have amazing taste in music.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.130
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.680
- I mean, who are some of your
favorites and inspirations?

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.340
- So many, I think.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.360
One of the first songs
my mom ever played me

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.823
was Etta James "At last"
and Patsy Cline, "Crazy",

00:01:53.823 --> 00:01:54.803
(audience clap)

00:01:54.803 --> 00:01:56.777
- [Drew] Dolly Parton?

00:01:56.777 --> 00:01:58.743
- Don't get me started on Dolly.

00:02:00.205 --> 00:02:02.480
Dolly's my favorite to this day.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.330
I love her so much.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.590
I love Carly Simon.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.040
I love Joni Mitchell, yeah.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.590
- I mean, who, how did you find?

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:11.860
You have amazing taste in music.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.700
- Thank you.
- How did you find it?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.310
- I think throughout the years,

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.900
honestly, if anything, I feel
like I've really come back

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.713
to artists like Joni and
Carole King, and Marvin Gaye.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.860
There's so many incredible artists

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.110
that I just really gravitate

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.280
towards the way it makes you feel.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.160
And the instrumentation of their songs

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.520
just kind of makes me feel
like elevated and alive.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.353
So I don't know,

00:02:36.353 --> 00:02:38.603
I guess just like through searching.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.750
- You are always in songwriting mode

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.620
and you're very prolific.
- [Sabrina] Thanks.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.960
- And you attack it in the moment.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.290
One of the reasons I fell
in love with this story

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.170
about you is it felt like
inspiration not lost.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.720
How do you remain in
constant songwriting mode?

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.380
How do you capture it?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.653
What is that life?

00:03:05.177 --> 00:03:07.450
- It's interesting 'cause
I'm a little paranoid

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.280
because I am always really
listening to the things

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.240
that people are saying,
sometimes maybe too in depth.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.830
- Like on social media,
or live and in person?

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.130
- Oh, I would say more live and in person,

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.000
social media, scary.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.110
I think live and in person,

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:26.020
you really get this unfiltered
version of conversations

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.510
and things that people aren't
necessarily calculating

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:30.343
before they say

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.800
so you'll have really,
really honest thoughts

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.787
and sometimes things that you go,

00:03:34.787 --> 00:03:36.730
"Oh, I can never say
that to a real person."

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.120
Or, "I can never put that in a song."

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.550
And I think that's been
the main inspiration for me

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.660
is what are those moments

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.560
that we feel like we
shouldn't say or we can't say,

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.863
and those are usually the best songs.

00:03:46.863 --> 00:03:49.446
(upbeat music)

